course: dictionary
lesson: 6922
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Never carry packages or bags for strangers.» Here a package is a parcel: something wrapped up to carry or deliver. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: «Packaging is designed to sell: a shiny bottle can cost double while the shampoo inside is nearly the same.» Packaging means the box or wrapping, not the shampoo itself. The clues are shiny bottle and cost: the wrapping is what is being talked about.
explain: Package can also be a verb: to package something means to put it into a box or wrapping. Swap each meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
explain: «New look, same great taste» can mean a smaller package for the same price. Here a package is a box or packet in a shop. The clue is the price: you pay the same but get less inside.
fact: A package is a parcel: something wrapped or boxed so it can be posted or delivered.
fact: In a shop, a package can be a packet or box of something, such as «a package of cookies».
fact: A package can also be a set of things offered together, such as «a holiday package».
fact: As a verb, «package» means to put something into a box or wrapping, and «packaged» is the past form.
fact: Useful phrases: package holiday, package deal, care package.
exercise: «Never carry packages or bags for strangers.» What is a package here? | A sweet | A type of holiday | A kind of drawing | *A parcel or wrapped thing
exercise: Each package holds 6 rolls. How many rolls are in 4 packages? | *24 | 46 | 64 | 10
exercise: To package something means what? | To count coins in a pile | To run very fast | To open a box and throw it away | *To put it into a box or wrapping
test: «Packaging is designed to sell.» In this sentence, what does packaging mean? | *The box or wrapping around a product | A shop that sells shampoo | A number of rolls in a pack | A holiday for two people
test: Which phrase means a set of things offered together, such as a holiday with everything arranged? | care package wrapped | packaged stone | *package holiday | open package
exam: In «Never open a suspicious package», what does package mean? | To wrap something up neatly | A sweet treat in a shop | A holiday you have booked | *A parcel that might be dangerous
